abstract: >-
  A satellite remote-sensing study testing whether Solar-Induced Fluorescence
  (SIF) signals agricultural drought earlier than NDVI in the eight districts
  of Marathwada, Maharashtra, over nine Kharif seasons (2015-2023), comparing
  cropland-weighted GOSIF v2 SIF with MODIS NDVI timed to each pixel's
  observation date. Standardised against normal years, the SIF and NDVI
  drought alarms fell within one 8-day composite of each other: both crossed
  z < -3 on the same date in 2015 and NDVI was eight days earlier in 2018;
  across 15 drought district-years SIF was earlier in 7, the same in 2 and
  NDVI earlier in 3, and the direction of these one-composite differences
  changes with how NDVI is dated. Scaled over the whole
  season, SIF's normal decline came before NDVI's in all nine years (8.0-34.2
  days), but NDVI does not return to its pre-season level after the monsoon;
  scaled from peak to post-peak minimum the lead falls to -5.5 to +13.4 days,
  is absent in three years, and district differences disappear (Friedman
  p = 0.97). MODIS NIRv and EVI lead NDVI as much as GOSIF does and GOSIF
  does not lead NIRv, so for GOSIF the remaining lead is a property of NDVI;
  TROPOMI SIF (2018-2020), not built from MODIS reflectance, declined first
  against NDVI and also slightly before NIRv. Only
  2015 and 2018 met the CHIRPS rainfall drought criterion; applied unchanged
  to 2001-2014 (five more drought years) as an out-of-sample test, the methods
  gave the same district-level picture (at z < -1.5, SIF earlier in 5 of 22
  drought district-years flagged by both, the same in 11, NDVI earlier in 6),
  while regionally SIF
  flagged two of five drought years at z < -3 and NDVI one. Reconstructed from
  India's Manual for Drought Management on CHIRPS rainfall, the rainfall-based
  Trigger-1 flagged 7 of 15 drought district-years (10 per pixel) with one false
  alarm in 57 normal district-years, before the satellite alarms wherever both
  fired; against crop loss it flagged 7 of 18 poor-harvest district-years with
  no false alarm, NDVI 13 and the two together 14, and the official 2018
  declaration covered districts the reconstruction missed. A three-week instead
  of four-week dry spell flags 14 and 26 normal ones. In this dataset GOSIF SIF
  is not a resolvably earlier drought alarm than NDVI, and its seasonal lead is
  largely a property of how NDVI's decline is measured.
keywords:
  - solar-induced fluorescence
  - GOSIF
